/*
Detection Rule: AWS EC2 Resource Hijacking for Cryptomining
Author: Bryan Jorge
MITRE ATT&CK: T1496 - Resource Hijacking
Severity: High
Description: Detects the launch of EC2 instances using GPU-optimized or
compute-intensive instance types commonly used for cryptomining (p3, p4,
g4, g5 families), or mass instance launches by a single principal across
multiple regions within a short window. Resource hijacking is one of the
most financially damaging outcomes of AWS credential theft — attackers
can accumulate thousands of dollars in charges within hours.
*/

index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
    eventSource="ec2.amazonaws.com"
    eventName="RunInstances"
    errorCode=""

| eval actor=coalesce(userIdentity.userName, userIdentity.principalId)
| eval instance_type=requestParameters.instanceType
| eval instance_count=coalesce(requestParameters.maxCount, 1)
| eval ami_id=requestParameters.imageId
| eval key_pair=requestParameters.keyName

/* Classify instance families by mining potential */
| eval is_gpu_instance=if(
    match(instance_type, "^p2|^p3|^p4|^g3|^g4|^g5|^gr6"), 1, 0)

| eval is_compute_heavy=if(
    match(instance_type, "^c5n|^c6in|^hpc|^x2|^u-"), 1, 0)

| eval is_mining_candidate=if(
    is_gpu_instance=1 OR is_compute_heavy=1, 1, 0)

/* Aggregate over 1-hour windows per actor */
| bin _time span=1h
| stats
    sum(instance_count)      AS total_instances,
    count                    AS launch_events,
    dc(awsRegion)            AS distinct_regions,
    values(instance_type)    AS instance_types,
    values(awsRegion)        AS regions,
    values(ami_id)           AS amis_used,
    values(sourceIPAddress)  AS source_ips,
    max(is_mining_candidate) AS mining_type_detected,
    min(_time)               AS first_seen,
    max(_time)               AS last_seen
    by actor, _time

| where mining_type_detected=1
    OR total_instances >= 10
    OR (distinct_regions >= 3 AND total_instances >= 5)

/* Score based on instance type, volume, and geographic spread */
| eval risk_score=0
| eval risk_score=if(mining_type_detected=1 AND distinct_regions >= 3, risk_score+65, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(mining_type_detected=1 AND total_instances >= 5,  risk_score+50, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(total_instances >= 20 AND distinct_regions >= 2,  risk_score+55, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(mining_type_detected=1,                           risk_score+35, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(total_instances >= 10,                            risk_score+25, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(distinct_regions >= 3,                            risk_score+15, risk_score)

| eval alert_title="EC2 Resource Hijacking / Cryptomining Suspected: " . actor
| table _time, alert_title, actor, total_instances, launch_events,
        distinct_regions, instance_types, regions, amis_used,
        source_ips, mining_type_detected, risk_score, first_seen, last_seen
| sort -risk_score

/*
TUNING PARAMETERS:
- total_instances threshold: Raise to 20 in environments with active autoscaling
- distinct_regions threshold: Raise if your org legitimately deploys to 3+ regions
- mining_type_detected filter: Add | where mining_type_detected=1 to limit to
  confirmed GPU/compute types only and eliminate volume-based false positives
- Whitelist examples:
  | where NOT match(actor, "SageMakerRole|MLTrainingRole|HPCRole|RenderFarm")
  | where NOT match(instance_types, "^t|^m|^r")

FALSE POSITIVES:
- ML/AI workloads legitimately using GPU instances for SageMaker training jobs
- HPC research workloads using compute-intensive instances for simulation
- Autoscaling events triggered by legitimate application load spikes
- Rendering pipelines (VFX, media) using GPU fleets for production work

RECOMMENDED RESPONSE:
1. Identify the launched instances and verify current state (running/stopped)
2. Confirm whether the actor has a legitimate business need for these instance types
3. Check running processes on suspicious instances via Systems Manager Session Manager
4. If mining confirmed: terminate all instances and disable actor's IAM credentials
5. Apply SCP to restrict GPU instance types in non-approved accounts
6. Audit AWS billing for unexpected charges and initiate cost dispute if warranted

INVESTIGATION QUERIES:
- All instances launched by actor: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  eventName="RunInstances" userIdentity.userName=<actor> earliest=-24h
  | table _time, requestParameters.instanceType, requestParameters.maxCount, awsRegion
- Running process check (via Systems Manager): requires SSM Agent on instance
  aws ssm send-command --document-name AWS-RunShellScript --parameters
  '{"commands":["ps aux | grep -E \"xmrig|cgminer|ethminer|monero\""]}' --instance-ids <id>
- Cost spike check: index=aws_billing earliest=-7d | stats sum(UnblendedCost) by LinkedAccountId, ServiceCode

DATA SOURCES REQUIRED:
- AWS CloudTrail (management events) — all active regions
- AWS Cost and Usage Reports (for billing anomaly correlation)

HIGH-RISK INDICATORS:
- Instances launched across 3+ regions simultaneously (maximizing hash rate)
- AMI ID is not from the organization's approved AMI catalog
- No key pair specified (instances may be controlled via user data script with embedded key)
- Actor's credentials were recently used from an anomalous geolocation

PREVENTION MEASURES:
- Set AWS Service Quotas to limit GPU instance counts to approved maximums
- Enable AWS Cost Anomaly Detection with threshold alerts for daily spend
- Apply SCP: Deny RunInstances for p*/g*/c5n* instance types in non-production accounts
- Enable GuardDuty: CryptoCurrency:EC2/BitcoinTool.B!DNS finding

RELATED TECHNIQUES:
- T1078.004 - Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts
- T1552.005 - Cloud Instance Metadata API
- T1059 - Command and Scripting Interpreter (via user data scripts)

CHANGELOG:
v1.0 (2026-02-17): Initial release
*/
